//
// Gate E cell: `assert(delete(p), …)` over a `FileResult` converts the condition to a boolean,
// a plain enum's truth its ordinal's (`OpConvBoolFromEnum`, `convert`'s `conv_bool_call`).
// @FR-E-Assert: `assert(c, m)` continues when its condition holds.
// @FR-E-Truthy-1: a present plain enum value is true in the assert condition.
// Prints:

fn main() {
  p = "zz_probe_assert_enum.txt";
  f = file(p); f.write("x");
  assert(delete(p), "cleanup");
}
